# Test: ze help ai <section> -- canonical AI reference grammar (subcommand form)
# VALIDATES: ze help ai api reaches the daemon API listing through dispatchHelp;
#            ze help ai self-describes its sections; the top-level usage signposts
#            the leaf; the legacy --ai flag alias still resolves.

# Canonical subcommand form reaches the daemon API endpoint listing.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze help ai api:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=Daemon API Commands
expect=stdout:contains=ze-show:

# Summary self-describes: lists the available sections including dispatch.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze help ai:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=Sections
expect=stdout:contains=dispatch

# Legacy flag alias still resolves to the same listing (backward compatibility).
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze help --ai api:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=ze-show:

# Discoverability: the top-level usage signposts the AI reference leaf.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze --help:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=help ai
# // dropped the seq=5 "ze --ai" self-correcting-hint assertion with
# the aiSectionGuess feature it covered; the hint was reverted as redundant with
# the usage signpost above (seq=4 still proves the leaf is discoverable).
